      <item>
        <title>AlphaFold 4: full protein complex prediction including ligands + nucleic acids + lipids</title>
        <link>https://deepmind.com/alphafold-4</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://deepmind.com/alphafold-4</guid>
        <pubDate>Fri, 22 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>DeepMind blog</source>
        <description>AlphaFold 4 is DeepMind&#x27;s 4th-generation protein structure predictor. The key upgrade: full complex prediction including small-molecule ligands, DNA, RNA, and lipids — not just proteins. The model uses a diffusion-based architecture with a unified tokeniser for all molecular types. On CASP17, AlphaFold 4 achieves GDT_TS 0.94 for single chains (vs AF3 0.87, ESM-4 0.92) and 0.89 for multi-chain complexes (vs AF3 0.82). On the PoseBench-2027 benchmark (protein-ligand binding pose), AF4 achieves 0.93 Top-1 accuracy (vs AF3 0.85, AutoDock Vina 0.61). Released via AlphaFold Server (free for non-commercial) + Isomorphic Cloud API (commercial). The model handles complexes up to 5000 residues + 50 ligands in a single prediction.</description>
        <category>Biology - Protein structure</category>
        <dc:creator>DeepMind Isomorphic Sciences</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>NVIDIA Earth-3: 10km global climate + 1km regional weather in a unified digital twin</title>
        <link>https://blogs.nvidia.com/earth-3-2027</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://blogs.nvidia.com/earth-3-2027</guid>
        <pubDate>Wed, 20 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>NVIDIA blog</source>
        <description>Earth-3 is NVIDIA&#x27;s 3rd-generation climate+weather digital twin. It unifies global climate simulation (10km resolution, 100-year projections) with regional weather forecasting (1km resolution, 14-day forecasts) in a single model — the first to bridge the climate-weather gap. Climate mode: 100-year global projection at 10km in 6 hours (vs 6 months for CMIP6 models). Weather mode: 14-day regional forecast at 1km in 2 minutes (vs 45 minutes for HRRR). Both modes share the same PINN backbone (Modulus v3, 50B params). Released via Earth-3 Cloud. 67 national weather services use the weather mode; 34 climate research institutions use the climate mode for IPCC AR8 contributions.</description>
        <category>Physics - Climate + weather digital twin</category>
        <dc:creator>NVIDIA + NOAA + ECMWF + JMA</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Claude 5 Ultra: 3T-param reasoning model — solves Riemann hypothesis (conditional)</title>
        <link>https://anthropic.com/claude-5-ultra</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://anthropic.com/claude-5-ultra</guid>
        <pubDate>Sun, 24 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Anthropic blog</source>
        <description>Claude 5 Ultra is Anthropic&#x27;s 3-trillion-parameter (MoE 1024 experts, top-16 routing) ultra-reasoning model. The &#x27;Ultra&#x27; variant extends Claude 5 Opus&#x27;s thinking budget from 1M to 10M tokens, enabling multi-day deductive reasoning. Active params: ~120B per token. On ARC-AGI-2, Claude 5 Ultra scores 0.91 (approaching the human-expert threshold of 0.95). On the Riemann Hypothesis Challenge (RH-2027), Claude 5 Ultra produced a 47-page proof that passes 8 of 10 verification checks — the closest any AI has come to solving a Millennium Prize problem. The 2 failing checks are in the analytic continuation step — the proof assumes a conjecture about L-functions that is itself unproven. Anthropic estimates that Claude 6 (with 100M-token thinking) could complete the proof. Released via API; cost: $500 per 1M thinking tokens.</description>
        <category>CS - Ultra reasoning</category>
        <dc:creator>Anthropic Research</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Llama 5: 1T-param open-weight MoE (Apache 2.0) — matches Claude 5 at 1/10th the cost</title>
        <link>https://ai.meta.com/llama-5</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://ai.meta.com/llama-5</guid>
        <pubDate>Sat, 23 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>Meta AI blog</source>
        <description>Llama 5 is Meta&#x27;s 1-trillion-parameter (MoE 256 experts, top-8 routing) open-weight LLM. Released under Apache 2.0 — the largest fully-open model ever. On MMLU-Pro, Llama 5 scores 0.89 (matching Claude 5&#x27;s 0.89, beating GPT-5&#x27;s 0.85). On HumanEval-Plus, Llama 5 scores 0.93 (beating Claude 5&#x27;s 0.91). The 256-expert MoE means only ~80B params active per token (top-8 of 256 experts × ~4B/expert). Deployable on a single NVIDIA B200 (192 GB HBM3e). The model was trained on 15T tokens of curated text + code + math. Released as 4 variants: Llama 5 Mini (8B, on-device), Llama 5 Small (70B), Llama 5 Medium (400B), Llama 5 Max (1T). All Apache 2.0. The Max variant matches closed models at 1/10th the API cost.</description>
        <category>CS - Open-weight LLM</category>
        <dc:creator>Meta AI</dc:creator>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>IBM Condor 2: 100,000-qubit superconducting quantum computer with 1000 logical qubits</title>
        <link>https://research.ibm.com/condor-2</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://research.ibm.com/condor-2</guid>
        <pubDate>Tue, 19 Jan 2027 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
        <source>IBM Research blog</source>
        <description>IBM Condor 2 is a 100,000-qubit superconducting quantum processor (transmon, 4K dilution refrigerator). The world&#x27;s first 100k-qubit quantum computer. Modular architecture: 100 tiles of 1000 qubits each, coupled via cryogenic microwave links. Condor 2 runs a distance-11 surface code (121 data + 120 ancilla = 241 qubits per logical qubit) achieving 10^-5 logical error rate. The 100k physical qubits support ~1000 logical qubits — sufficient for fault-tolerant quantum chemistry (FeMoco at chemical accuracy) and combinatorial optimisation (1000-variable QUBO). Available via IBM Quantum Cloud. 200+ research groups. The modular tile architecture enables scaling to 1M qubits (Condor 3, planned 2029) by adding more tiles.</description>
        <category>Physics - 100k-qubit quantum</category>
        <dc:creator>IBM Quantum</dc:creator>
      </item>
